## What I Built

### Organizational Unit (OU) Structure
Designed a department-based OU hierarchy mirroring a real org:

```
lab.local
├── IT
│   └── ServiceAccounts
├── HR
├── Finance
└── Servers
```

### Users & Groups
- Created 10+ domain user accounts distributed across OUs
- Built security groups: `IT-Admins`, `HR-Staff`, `Finance-ReadOnly`
- Assigned users to groups following least-privilege principles

### Group Policy Objects (GPOs)
| GPO | Scope | Settings Applied |
|---|---|---|
| Default Domain Policy | Domain-wide | Password complexity, min length 12, 90-day expiry, history 10 |
| HR-Desktop-Policy | HR OU | CMD access disabled, desktop items hidden |

### Automated User Provisioning (PowerShell)
Wrote a PowerShell script to bulk-create users from a CSV file, placing each account in the correct OU with appropriate group membership — simulating a real joiner workflow.

```powershell
Import-Module ActiveDirectory

# Import CSV
$Users = Import-Csv ".\new-users.csv"

foreach ($User in $Users) {

    try {

        # Build OU path dynamically
        $OUPath = "OU=$($User.Department),DC=lab,DC=local"

        # Convert password
        $SecurePassword = ConvertTo-SecureString $User.Password -AsPlainText -Force

        # Create AD User
        New-ADUser `
            -Name $User.Name `
            -GivenName $User.FirstName `
            -Surname $User.LastName `
            -SamAccountName $User.Username `
            -UserPrincipalName "$($User.Username)@lab.local" `
            -Department $User.Department `
            -Title $User.Title `
            -EmailAddress $User.Email `
            -Path $OUPath `
            -AccountPassword $SecurePassword `
            -Enabled $true `
            -ChangePasswordAtLogon $true `
            -PasswordNeverExpires $false

        Write-Host "[SUCCESS] Created user: $($User.Username)" -ForegroundColor Green

        # Add user to security group
        Add-ADGroupMember `
            -Identity $User.Group `
            -Members $User.Username

        Write-Host "[SUCCESS] Added $($User.Username) to group $($User.Group)" -ForegroundColor Cyan

    }
    catch {

        Write-Host "[ERROR] Failed to create user: $($User.Username)" -ForegroundColor Red
        Write-Host $_.Exception.Message

    }
}
```

